During Final 4→Final 3 transition, race conditions from duplicate event handlers were triggering an extra eviction, leaving only 2 players instead of 3. Console logs showed multiple duplicate call warnings across fast-forward, social maneuvers, and AI scheduler modules.

## Changes

### Guard flags in `js/veto.js`
- Added `__f4ToF3TransitionStarted` guard to `proceedAfterFinal4Eviction()` to prevent duplicate transition attempts
- Added same flag check to `finalizeFinal4Eviction()` to block eviction after transition starts
- Flag persists after cleanup to maintain race protection

```javascript
function proceedAfterFinal4Eviction(){
  var g = global.game;

  // Guard to prevent duplicate transitions
  if(g.__f4ToF3TransitionStarted) {
    console.warn('[Final4] Transition to Final 3 already started, ignoring duplicate call');
    return;
  }
  g.__f4ToF3TransitionStarted = true;
  // ... cleanup and transition
}
```

### Player count validation in `js/competitions.js`
- Added defensive validation in `startFinal3Flow()` to verify exactly 3 players present
- Edge case handling: 2 players→jury vote, >3 players→error log and return
- Provides safety net if guards fail to prevent race condition

```javascript
function startFinal3Flow() {
  const alive = global.alivePlayers();

  if(alive.length !== 3) {
    console.error('[F3] startFinal3Flow called with wrong player count:', alive.length);
    if(alive.length === 2) {
      setTimeout(() => global.startJuryVote?.(), 300);
      return;
    }
    return;
  }
  // ... continue with Final 3 flow
}
```

## Test coverage
Added `test_final4_guards.html` with unit tests for guard flag behavior and player count validation logic.

