> ## Bug Description
> 
> After recent PRs (from today), the game started to bug in the Final 3 part. The console shows:
> 
> ```
> [F3P1] Only 1 losers available (expected 2). Continuing with available players.
> ```
> 
> This indicates that when `startFinal3Flow()` is called, there are only 2 players remaining instead of 3. One player has been incorrectly evicted before the Final 3 flow properly starts.
> 
> ## Root Cause Analysis
> 
> The console logs show multiple "duplicate call" warnings:
> - `[ff] Fast-forward already active, ignoring duplicate call`
> - `[social-maneuvers] onSocialPhaseEnd already called - ignoring duplicate`
> - `[social-ai-autostart] Already running - ignoring duplicate start`
> 
> This suggests race conditions where multiple event handlers are firing, and one of them is triggering an unwanted eviction during the Final 4 → Final 3 transition.
> 
> ## Required Fixes
> 
> ### 1. Add guard flag to `proceedAfterFinal4Eviction()` in `js/veto.js`
> 
> The function needs a guard to ensure it only runs once. Add at the beginning of the function:
> 
> ```javascript
